@startuml SD_Admin_Product_CRUD
!theme cerulean-outline

title Admin Product CRUD Lifecycle\nAdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

actor       "Admin"              as Admin
participant "Browser / React\n(Admin Page)"  as React      #LightBlue
participant "Axios\napiClient"                as Axios      #LightCyan
participant "Controllers\n[Authorize(Roles=\"Admin\")]" as Controller #LightGreen
participant "ProductRepository"               as Repo       #LightYellow
participant "OltpDbContext\n(SQL Server\nAdventureWorks2019)" as DB #LightPink

note over Axios
  All requests include:
  Authorization: Bearer {token}
  (via Axios interceptor)
end note

== Step 1: Load Admin Page Data ==

Admin -> React : Navigates to Admin Products page
React -> React : useEffect triggers\nparallel data load

par Load categories and products
    React -> Axios : CatalogService.getCategories()
    Axios -> Controller : **GET /api/categories**
    Controller -> DB : _db.Categories.OrderBy(Name)
    DB --> Controller : Category[]
    Controller --> Axios : **200 OK** Category[]
    Axios --> React : categories

    React -> Axios : CatalogService.getProducts()
    Axios -> Controller : **GET /api/products**
    Controller -> Repo : GetAllAsync()
    Repo -> DB : SELECT Products\nINCLUDE Category, SubCategory\nORDER BY Name
    DB --> Repo : Product[]
    Repo --> Controller : Product[]
    Controller --> Axios : **200 OK** ProductDto[]
    Axios --> React : products
end

React -> React : Render product table\nwith Edit/Delete buttons\nand "Add Product" form
React --> Admin : Admin product management\npage displayed

== Step 2: Create Product ==

Admin -> React : Fills create form:\nSku, Name, Description,\nPrice, StockQty, CategoryId,\nSubCategoryId
Admin -> React : Clicks **"Add Product"**

React -> Axios : CatalogService.createProduct(productData)
Axios -> Controller : **POST /api/products**\nBody: CreateProductDto

Controller -> Controller : [Authorize(Roles="Admin")]\nvalidate Admin role

Controller -> Repo : ExistsBySkuAsync(dto.Sku)
Repo -> DB : SELECT ANY WHERE Sku = @sku
DB --> Repo : true / false

alt SKU already exists
    Repo --> Controller : true
    Controller --> Axios : **400 Bad Request**\n"SKU already exists."
    Axios --> React : Show error
else SKU is unique
    Repo --> Controller : false

    Controller -> Controller : Build Product entity
    Controller -> Repo : AddAsync(entity)
    Repo -> DB : INSERT INTO Products\n(CategoryId, Description,\nImageFileName, Name, Price,\nSku, StockQty, SubCategoryId)\nVALUES (...)
    note right of DB : Uses raw SQL to bypass\nEF Core @@ROWCOUNT issue\nwith INSTEAD OF INSERT trigger
    DB --> Repo : OK
    Repo -> DB : SELECT WHERE Sku = @sku\n(get generated Id)
    DB --> Repo : Product with Id
    Repo --> Controller : created entity

    Controller -> Repo : GetByIdAsync(id)
    Repo -> DB : SELECT with Includes
    DB --> Repo : Product
    Controller --> Axios : **201 Created**\nProductDto + Location header
    Axios --> React : newProduct
    React -> React : Add to product list\nRefresh table
    React --> Admin : New product appears in table
end

== Step 3: Upload Product Image ==

Admin -> React : Clicks **"Upload Image"**\non product row
Admin -> React : Selects image file\n(PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, max 20MB)

React -> Axios : CatalogService.uploadProductImage(id, file)
React -> React : Build FormData:\nformData.append("file", file)

Axios -> Controller : **POST /api/products/{id}/image**\nContent-Type: multipart/form-data\nBody: FormData with file
note right of Controller : [Consumes("multipart/form-data")]\n[RequestSizeLimit(20_000_000)]

Controller -> Repo : GetByIdAsync(id)
Repo -> DB : SELECT Product
DB --> Repo : Product

alt Product not found
    Controller --> Axios : **404 Not Found**
else Product found
    Controller -> Controller : Validate file extension:\n.png, .jpg, .jpeg, .gif

    alt Invalid file type
        Controller --> Axios : **400 Bad Request**\n"Invalid file type."
    else Valid file type
        opt Old image exists
            Controller -> Controller : Delete old image file:\nFile.Delete(oldPath)
        end

        Controller -> Controller : Generate filename:\nproduct-{id}-{guid}{ext}
        Controller -> Controller : Save to disk:\nC:\\images\\product\\{filename}
        note right of Controller : Directory.CreateDirectory(root)\nensures path exists

        Controller -> Repo : UpdateAsync(product)\nproduct.ImageFileName = newFilename
        Repo -> DB : UPDATE Products\nSET ImageFileName = @name\nWHERE Id = @id
        DB --> Repo : OK

        Controller -> Repo : GetByIdAsync(id)
        Repo -> DB : SELECT with Includes
        DB --> Repo : Updated product
        Controller --> Axios : **200 OK** ProductDto\n(with new ImageFileName)
        Axios --> React : updatedProduct
        React -> React : Update product in list\nImage thumbnail refreshes
        React --> Admin : Product image updated
    end
end

== Step 4: Update Product ==

Admin -> React : Clicks **"Edit"** on product row
React -> React : Open edit form\npre-filled with current values
Admin -> React : Modifies fields\nClicks **"Save"**

React -> Axios : CatalogService.updateProduct(id, data)
Axios -> Controller : **PUT /api/products/{id}**\nBody: CreateProductDto

Controller -> Repo : GetByIdAsync(id)
Repo -> DB : SELECT Product
DB --> Repo : Product

alt Product not found
    Controller --> Axios : **404 Not Found**
else Product found
    Controller -> Repo : ExistsBySkuAsync(sku, exceptId: id)
    Repo -> DB : ANY WHERE Sku = @sku AND Id != @id
    DB --> Repo : true / false

    alt SKU conflict
        Controller --> Axios : **400 Bad Request**\n"SKU already exists."
    else SKU OK
        Controller -> Controller : Update entity fields:\nSku, Name, Description,\nPrice, StockQty, ImageFileName,\nCategoryId, SubCategoryId

        Controller -> Repo : UpdateAsync(product)
        Repo -> DB : UPDATE Products SET ...\nWHERE Id = @id
        note right of DB : Raw SQL bypasses\nINSTEAD OF UPDATE trigger issue
        DB --> Repo : OK

        Controller --> Axios : **204 No Content**
        Axios --> React : Success
        React -> React : Refresh product list
        React --> Admin : Product updated in table
    end
end

== Step 5: Delete Product ==

Admin -> React : Clicks **"Delete"** on product row
React -> React : Confirmation dialog:\n"Delete this product?"
Admin -> React : Confirms deletion

React -> Axios : CatalogService.deleteProduct(id)
Axios -> Controller : **DELETE /api/products/{id}**

Controller -> Repo : GetByIdAsync(id)
Repo -> DB : SELECT Product
DB --> Repo : Product

alt Product not found
    Controller --> Axios : **404 Not Found**
else Product found
    Controller -> Repo : DeleteAsync(product)
    Repo -> DB : DELETE FROM Products\nWHERE Id = @id

    alt Foreign key constraint (referenced by OrderItems)
        DB --> Repo : DbUpdateException
        Repo --> Controller : throws DbUpdateException
        Controller --> Axios : **409 Conflict**\n"Product cannot be deleted because\nit is referenced by existing order items."
        Axios --> React : Show error message
        React --> Admin : Error: "Cannot delete -\nreferenced by orders"
    else Delete succeeds
        DB --> Repo : OK
        Repo --> Controller : OK
        Controller --> Axios : **204 No Content**
        Axios --> React : Success
        React -> React : Remove product from list
        React --> Admin : Product removed from table
    end
end

@enduml
